{# ON THIS PAGE — the index a page carries left of its sections, and the grid
   that holds both. The design's (DesignsProjects/team-module/vendor/
   house-index.css + house-index.js, used on variants-permissions-pages/
   analysis.html); behaviour in assets/controllers/onpage_controller.js.

   A PAGE WRITES NONE OF ITS MARKUP. It embeds this partial with its rows and
   puts its sections in the one block; each section carries the id its row
   names:

     {% embed '@Shell/_onpage.html.twig' with {rows: [
         {id: 'drift', label: 'Drift', count: 3},
         {head: 'Lists'},
         {id: 'vacant', label: 'Vacant positions'},
     ]} only %}
         {% block shell_onpage_main %}
             <div class="c" id="drift">…</div>
             <div class="c" id="vacant">…</div>
         {% endblock %}
     {% endembed %}

   PARAMETERS:
     rows   in page order: {id, label, count?, title?} one row per section —
            a count of null draws none, and zero is a count; a title is the
            row's tooltip — or {head} for a head between rows
     label  the index's own name; "On this page" unless a page has a better one

   AN EMBED, NOT AN INCLUDE, because the index and the sections share one
   grid and an include cannot wrap a page's content: "The embed tag combines
   the behaviour of include and extends. It allows you to include another
   template's contents, just like include does. But it also allows you to
   override any block defined inside the included template".
   https://twig.symfony.com/doc/3.x/tags/embed.html —
   vendor/twig/twig/src/TokenParser/EmbedTokenParser.php.

   THE SNIPPET COMES FIRST. It stamps html.onpage-closed before the grid is
   parsed, from the remembered choice or a viewport of 900px or narrower, so
   the index is never painted open and then collapsed. It is written here
   rather than in the document, so a page without an index carries none of
   it. The key and the width are the controller's. #}
{%- set _label = label|default('On this page') -%}
{%- set _name = 'uhifadhi--shell-bundle--onpage' -%}
<script>(function(){var c=false;try{c=localStorage.getItem('uhifadhi-pp-nav')==='closed'}catch(e){}if(c||window.matchMedia('(max-width:900px)').matches){document.documentElement.classList.add('onpage-closed')}})()</script>
<div class="onpage">
    <nav class="onpage-nav" aria-label="{{ _label }}" data-controller="{{ _name }}" data-action="click->{{ _name }}#go">
        <div class="onpage-top"><p class="onpage-h">{{ _label }}</p><button type="button" class="onpage-tg" aria-expanded="true" aria-label="Collapse index" title="Collapse index" data-{{ _name }}-target="toggle" data-action="click->{{ _name }}#toggle">{{ ux_icon('shell:chevrons-left', {'aria-hidden': 'true'}) }}</button></div>
        {%- for row in rows %}
            {%- if row.head is defined %}
        <p class="onpage-h">{{ row.head }}</p>
            {%- else %}
        <a class="onpage-row" href="#{{ row.id|url_encode }}"{% if row.title ?? null %} title="{{ row.title }}"{% endif %}><i class="onpage-dot" aria-hidden="true" title="{{ row.label }}"></i><span class="onpage-l">{{ row.label }}</span>{% if row.count is defined and row.count is not null %}<b class="onpage-n">{{ row.count }}</b>{% endif %}</a>
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
    </nav>
    <div class="onpage-main">{% block shell_onpage_main %}{% endblock %}</div>
</div>
